  "releaseNotes": "MFA TOTP/QR rotation now gated behind a verified email OTP (Purpose=ResetTotp). New ExbilCoreMFAStartResetTotpCommand to drive the recovery flow (lost-device path) — POST /api/tfa/start-reset-totp issues a single-use email OTP that must be verified before /api/tfa/setup-authenticator with ForceResetQrCode=true is allowed. ExbilCoreMfaInitDto now exposes CanResetOtpQrCode (fail-closed default false). Behavioural change: ExbilCoreAuthenticatorRequestModel.ForceResetQrCode default flipped from true to false (fail-closed) — callers that relied on the previous default must opt in explicitly when they really need a regenerate.",
